      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2018 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Asymmetric construction of tetrahydrothiophenes with four contiguous stereocenters remains a formidable challenge. Herein, the bottleneck was addressed by an unprecedented one-pot Michael-Henry-cascade-rearrangement reaction that could simultaneously create four consecutive stereogenic centers including two tetrasubstituted carbon stereocenters. The highly functionalized chiral spirotetrahydrothiophene scaffolds were assembled in moderate to good yields (≈54-79\u2009%), excellent diastereo- (>20:1 d.r.) and enantio-selectivities (up to 93\u2009% ee)."
      },
